From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tariq Bashir <tbashir@brightsign.biz>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:58:00 +0100
Subject: gpu: enable validating command decoder for BrightSign builds

BrightSign uses native EGL/GLES2 (not ANGLE) via the Nexus and Wayland
ozone backends. The passthrough command decoder requires ANGLE and
CHECK-fails in GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl::Initialize() when it
detects a non-ANGLE GL implementation.

Previously, enable_validating_command_decoder was only true for Android,
so on BrightSign (Linux) builds ENABLE_VALIDATING_COMMAND_DECODER was
false, forcing UsePassthroughCommandDecoder() to unconditionally return
true. This caused a SIGTRAP crash when MSE video playback created a new
GPU command buffer context.

Add is_brightsign to the enable_validating_command_decoder condition so
the validating decoder is available and correctly selected at runtime.

diff --git a/ui/gl/features.gni b/ui/gl/features.gni
index e0bdd667233d5e96f70587a381e8f05590f95adf..7844bf37784bb07158f4aef6273e375129932ee0 100644
--- a/ui/gl/features.gni
+++ b/ui/gl/features.gni
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 # found in the LICENSE file.
 
+import("//build/config/brightsign_build.gni")
 import("//build/config/cast.gni")
 import("//build/config/chrome_build.gni")
 
@@ -20,7 +21,7 @@ declare_args() {
   # Independent of use_dawn, which controls whether Dawn is used in Chromium.
   build_dawn_tests = is_mac || is_win || is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android
 
-  enable_validating_command_decoder = is_android
+  enable_validating_command_decoder = is_android || is_brightsign
 }
 
 declare_args() {
